scope: |
  Two of the corpus contract's remaining reds, both filed by me, both on the v1 JS lane, and the
  evidence says ONE defect rather than two:

    examples/coroutine-demo.ssc            -> Error: not callable: ()
    examples/rozum-agent-schema-derived.ssc -> Error: not callable: ()

  Byte-identical message AND byte-identical operand: the generated `.cjs` is calling a value that
  evaluated to Unit. Fixing one should close both; if it does not, that itself is the finding and
  the second gets its own entry.

  Plan: reduce each to a minimal .ssc, check whether the two minimals coincide, then pin which
  codegen path emits `()` where a function belongs. Add ONE cross-lane conformance case (the JS
  lane must fail-first) — neither example is in a position to serve as the regression test, since
  both are large and one binds a real socket.

  Prerequisite already satisfied: the v1 JS backend is unclaimed (js-char-into-int-param released).
next: minimal repro for each, compare, then locate the emitter
